From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucaszhongsj <lucaszhongsj@foxmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 11:36:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ios/layout: portrait on an ordinary iPhone with a 16:9
 picture and a companion band

Allow portrait on the phone, give the picture the height its own width asks for (no bars on a 19.5:9 screen), keep a panel view under the pad in the band, and run handheld while the phone stands up so the game's own keyboard takes touches.

The picture never takes more than half the window, so an iPad's taller picture keeps the midpoint split it had; a Duo's fold still sets both edges. A console mode chosen in the in-game menu while standing up survives the return to landscape.

Front-end changes only: no host, rewriter or shader change. The Duo harness covers the split, the panel's place under the pad, orientation policy and the console mode switch (41 tests).

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: The ACNH companion: Eden Duo's reader and the band a phone standing up shows it in; nxnative carries it on feat/acnh-companion
Issue: none yet: no upstream issue for the companion

